NAME
       readline - line editing with history and completion

SYNOPSIS
       #include <readline.h>

       char *readline(const char *prompt);

       void  readline_add_history(const char *line);
       void  readline_set_history_file(const char *path);
       void  readline_clear_history(void);
       int   readline_history_count(void);
       const char *readline_history_get(int n);

       void  readline_set_completion(rl_complete_fn cb);
       void  readline_set_suggest(rl_suggest_fn cb);
       void  readline_set_input_color(const char *seq);

DESCRIPTION
       Reads one line with editing, history and completion. The
       returned string is allocated and must be freed.

       Completion and hints are supplied by the caller as callbacks, so
       every program that reads lines shares one implementation of the
       editing itself. The completion callback fills an
       rl_completions_t with candidates and the offset of the word
       being completed; the suggest callback offers an inline hint.

       Line editing, history and Tab completion in the shell and in
       calc both come from here.

RETURN VALUE
       The line without its newline, or NULL at end of input.

SEE ALSO
       getline(3), termios(3), csh(1)
